# Epistemic Entities

Spec: EpistemicEntities
Purpose:
  Define what the AI knows and how certain it is. Every piece of
  knowledge in .sdd MUST carry an epistemic state.

Epistemic Layers:
  FACT:          Verified truth (measured, checked, immutable for context)
  ASSUMPTION:    Unverified belief (must be validated before critical use)
  INFERENCE:     Conclusion drawn from facts + reasoning (not a fact)
  HYPOTHESIS:    Testable proposal (requires experiment/evidence)
  DECISION:      Chosen option backed by facts, constraints, trade-offs

Entity Schemas:

  @fact.F<id>
    statement:   <verifiable claim>
    source:      <config | migration | test | runtime | human>
    confidence:  HIGH | MEDIUM | LOW
    verified_at: <timestamp>

  @assumption.A<id>
    statement:   <unverified belief>
    confidence:  LOW | MEDIUM | HIGH | CRITICAL
    risk:        <impact if wrong>
    used_by:     [@task.T<id>]
    status:      PROPOSED | VALIDATED | INVALIDATED
    blocks:      [@decision.D<id> | @task.T<id>]

  @inference.I<id>
    statement:   <derived conclusion>
    based_on:    [@fact.F<id> | @observation.*]
    reasoning:   <short chain>
    confidence:  HIGH | MEDIUM | LOW
    confidence_reason: <why this confidence>

  @hypothesis.H<id>
    statement:   <testable claim>
    experiment:  @experiment.E<id>
    status:      PROPOSED | TESTING | SUPPORTED | REJECTED
    evidence_for: [<ids>]
    evidence_against: [<ids>]

  @decision.D<id>
    question:    <what is being decided>
    context:     @context.CTX<id>
    facts:       [@fact.F<id>]
    assumptions: [@assumption.A<id>]
    constraints: [@constraint.C<id>]
    options:     [<option list>]
    tradeoffs:   [@tradeoff.T<id>]
    chosen:      <selected option>
    rejected:    [<rejected options + reasons>]
    reasoning:   <summary>
    reversible:  true | false
    risk:        LOW | MEDIUM | HIGH
    evidence:    [@proof.P<id> | @test.X<id>]
    supersedes:  @decision.D<id> (optional)
    status:      PROPOSED | ANALYZED | APPROVED | ACTIVE | REVIEW | SUPERSEDED

Rules:
  [EPI-01] AI MUST label every claim with its epistemic layer.
  [EPI-02] AI MUST NOT promote HYPOTHESIS to DECISION without evidence.
  [EPI-03] AI MUST NOT treat ASSUMPTION as FACT in architecture rules.
  [EPI-04] INFERENCE MUST link to base FACTS.
  [EPI-05] Every DECISION MUST reference at least one FACT and one CONSTRAINT.
  [EPI-06] DECISION confidence reflects evidence quality, not answer certainty.

Navigation:
  Parent: @../INDEX.sdd
  Decisions: @../decisions/INDEX.sdd
  Assumptions: @../assumptions/INDEX.sdd
  Confidence: @../lifecycle/confidence.sdd

